                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "swivel-head":</h3><p>Mics tagged <b>swivel-head</b> have rotating or swiveling headbaskets. This can ease positioning of the microphone; for example, the body can be parallel to the shell of a drum, while the microphone capsule is rotated to point at the top head. Functionally, these mics can easily change from <em>end-adress</em> to <em>side-address</em>, with an infinite number of possible positions in between.</p><p>See also <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/tag/yoke-mount">yoke-mount</a> microphones, in which the entire microphone body swivels.</p>
